                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "So you like Binding of Issac, Nuclear Throne, Enter the Gungeon, etc? Well to be fair this game really doesn't do too much to separate itself from the rest of the crowd - not that that's a bad thing if you like those games I named. \n\nThe story is plain and simple you are transported into a videogame to save your sister - sounds easy enough, right? There are 5 areas (forest, dungeon, etc) each having increasingly tougher and more enemies. The levels are procedurally generated but you can retry a floor until you beat it which I felt was nice. The later levels actually were easier since you can buy guns and health upgrades. \n\nA couple negative points: 1) the game is short as you can see my playtime is just under 2 hours and 2) the final boss was a little simpler/easier than I would have liked.\n\nA couple positive points: 1) weapons variety is good (each has its own feel) 2) there is a bit of replayability via an arcade mode if that's you thing.\n\nSome closing thoughts: I imagine a lot of people will pass on this just given that it doesn't drop cards but honestly this is truly a gem at this price point. Hope this helps.",
